content.text:
Portrait title fits. But game frame at top with huge empty space below — could center it vertically in portrait instead of top; controls are inside frame bottom, so better center vertically? If centered, game sits middle, no controls elsewhere. Center would look better. But touch buttons at bottom of frame; with game centered, thumbs at bottom of screen far from frame? The touch controls are inside frame, so if centered, buttons are also centered vertically — awkward for thumbs. Top placement keeps buttons at ~y 200 while thumbs at 800. Hmm.

Better: in portrait, move #touch out of frame flow? Can't easily. Use fixed positioning relative to viewport on portrait:
```
@media (orientation: portrait) {
  #touch { position: fixed; inset: auto 0 0 0; padding: ...; z-index: 20; }
  #touch .tbtn { width 64px ... background more opaque }
}
```
Then buttons at bottom of screen, game at top. But distance large. Could place game vertically centered and buttons fixed bottom; nice: game in middle top-ish (~y 150-370), buttons at bottom y 750. Big gap but visible. Hmm ergonomically thumbs rest at bottom, that's good; eyes look up.

Alternatively, in portrait use a layout with game at top and touch controls right below the frame (not viewport bottom), still reachable if phone held. Frame ends at y~233; buttons at ~300; that's high for thumbs but okay. Use #touch position: static? It's inside frame absolute; could move with transform translateY(100%)? That would overlay content below frame but with stage parent.

Simplest good UX: fixed at bottom, large buttons, game centered? Let's set #app justify-content: space-between? Game at top 40px and controls bottom. That's common in portrait mobile games (controls at bottom, screen top). I'll move #touch fixed bottom and enlarge buttons. And maybe add a small "gira el móvil" hint below game.

However this is extra; landscape is main. Keep current? Buttons inside frame bottom in portrait are tiny and at top of screen. Not great.

Let me implement fixed touch controls in portrait:
```
@media (orientation: portrait) {
  #touch { position: fixed; inset: auto 0 0 0; z-index: 30; padding: 0 18px calc(18px+env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); }
  #touch .tbtn { width: 64px; height: 64px; font-size: 24px; }
  .tbtn-jump { width: 76px; height: 76px; }
  #top-buttons { ... maybe fixed top-right? }
}
```
But #touch is child of #frame with position fixed → fixed relative viewport despite overflow hidden? Fixed positioning inside element with transform/filter would be relative, but #frame has no transform (isolation only), and overflow hidden does not clip fixed. It works.

Also in portrait, hide #footer-hint already.

Test again.

Also need to test gameplay mobile with touch. Let's click start (button center) and screenshot.

Before that, fix mobile-touch class persistence after reload? We added manually. Actual touch browser gets it automatically.

Let's update CSS.

